

                        -=- CheckForNode v1.1 -=-


CheckForNode can only be used with FAME BBS Systems.

CheckForNode is designed to check if a specific FAME Node exists.

CheckForNode is normally located in 'FAME:Modules/CheckForNode'.

Template:

NODENR/K/N,LOCATION/K:

Usage:

CheckForNode NODENR=0 LOCATION=FAME:

If NODENR is not set CheckForNode will use 0 as default.
if LOCATION is not set CheckForNode will use 'FAME:' as default.

CheckForNode returns 0 if the Node has been found.
CheckForNode returns 50 (RETURN_FAIL / Fail) if the Node is not online.

You can use CheckForNode in a script as follows:

---------------------------------- Cut ----------------------------------
FailAt 100

FAME:Modules/CheckForNode

If Not Fail
	Echo "Node exists."
Else
	Echo "Node does not exist."
Endif
---------------------------------- Cut ----------------------------------


